ma-gpui/releases/download/v0.1.1/SHA256SUMS"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sina96/colima-gpui/tarball/v0.1.1","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sina96/colima-gpui/zipball/v0.1.1","body":"### Changed\n\n- Settings → About shows \"Up to date\" (or why the check failed) only after you click **Check for updates** or use **Check for Updates…**, and hides it again when you switch sections or close Settings.\n- A profile without the Docker runtime shows a short \"No Docker tabs\" note in the tab row, with the reason on hover, instead of a long sentence.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- The delete dialog's \"Also delete container data\" text wraps inside the dialog instead of running past its edge, and the dialog's message is shorter.\n\n## Install\n\nDownload the `.dmg` for your Mac: **arm64** for Apple silicon (M1 and later), **x86_64** for Intel. Open it and drag Colima GPUI to Applications.\n\nThe app isn't notarized by Apple yet. The first time you open it, macOS blocks it: open **System Settings → Privacy & Security** and click **Open Anyway**. See the [README](https://github.com/sina96/colima-gpui#install) for details.\n\nColima GPUI needs [Colima](https://github.com/abiosoft/colima#installation) and the Docker CLI: `brew install colima docker`.\n"}